>
  <p>Memoato is released under the <a href="https://github.com/hrvojepavlinovic/memoato-app/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT license</a>. You can inspect, modify, and self-host the code, subject to its license and third-party dependencies.</p>

  <h2>What is in the repository?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Personal memory</strong> — raw note capture, extraction, review, recall, categories, and timeline.</li>
    <li><strong>Context pilot</strong> — read-only GitHub and Linear sources, source versions, human claim review, and access and freshness checks.</li>
    <li><strong>API and MCP</strong> — scoped keys for logging, recall, and context packets.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The hosted Context pilot is limited to one owner per workspace. Open code does not mean open team signup.</p>

  <h2>Run your own instance</h2>
  <p>Start with the <a href="https://github.com/hrvojepavlinovic/memoato-app#readme" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository README</a> and <a href="https://github.com/hrvojepavlinovic/memoato-app/blob/main/docs/DEV_SETUP.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">development setup</a>. Self-hosting means operating the application and database, configuring providers, and maintaining backups and updates.</p>
  <p>Choose your storage mode and AI processing setup deliberately. Self-hosting alone does not stop a configured AI provider from receiving data. See the <a href="/privacy-first">storage and AI processing explanation</a>.</p>

  <h2>Contribute from real use</h2>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/hrvojepavlinovic/memoato-app/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">Report a reproducible issue</a>, suggest a clearer flow, or propose a code change. Keep private notes, source documents, and API keys out of public issues.</p>

